prompt:
ANIMATION SPRITE SHEET in the same 4 columns x 2 rows grid layout and cell size as the first attached sheet: 8 frames of the SAME basic zombie (brown torn suit jacket, white shirt, red necktie, blue ragged trousers, brown shoes, grey-green skin, big round eyes) doing a calm, lazy, rhythmic zombie GROOVE, head-bobbing to music, seen from the same three-quarter side view facing LEFT. Same size, same ground line and same horizontal placement in every cell; the whole zombie inside its cell.
IMPORTANT: this is a SUBTLE dance. In EVERY frame the feet stay planted side by side on the ground, the body stays upright (only slightly hunched), and both forearms are held loosely in front of the belly at waist height (elbows bent, hands hanging limp, like a zombie resting its arms). Only the head, the shoulders and the knees move a little. The frames loop:
1) upright, head tilted toward his LEFT shoulder;
2) knees slightly bent in a small bounce, head nodding forward, hands bobbing down a little;
3) upright, head straight, shoulders level;
4) knees slightly bent in a small bounce, head nodding forward;
5) upright, head tilted toward his RIGHT shoulder, mouth open with the tongue sticking out a little;
6) knees slightly bent in a small bounce, head nodding forward;
7) upright, head straight, shoulders shrugged up a little;
8) knees slightly bent in a small bounce, head nodding forward.
No raised arms, no reaching arms, no leg kicks, no hopping, no motion lines, no text, no shadows.
